  "text": "Clinical Trials | Cornell University College of Veterinary Medicine\nSkip to main content\nSearch:\nSubmit Search\nSearch Filters\nSearch\nThis Site\nSearch\nCornell\nMenu\nSearch Cornell\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine Home\nDirections\nContact Us\nEmergency\nPhone Numbers\nRoutine and Emergency Care\nCompanion Animal Hospital\nin Ithaca, NY for cats, dogs, exotics, and wildlife\n607.253.3060\nDirections\nEquine\nand\nNemo Farm Animal\nHospitals in Ithaca, NY for horses and farm animals\n607.253.3100\nDirections\nCornell Ruffian Equine Specialists, on Long Island\nfor every horse\n516.488.4510\nDirections\nAmbulatory and Production Medicine\nfor service on farms within 30 miles of Ithaca, NY\n607.253.3140\nDirections\nAnimal Health Diagnostic Center\nNew York State Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory\n607.253.3900\nDirections\nGeneral Information\nCornell University College of Veterinary Medicine\nIthaca, New York 14853-6401\n607.253.3000\nDirections\nQuestions?\nEmail Us\nEmergencies\nSupport Us\nHospitals\nComprehensive Care + 24 Hour Emergency\nHospitals\nCompanion Animal Hospital\nSmall Animal Community Practice\nEquine Hospital\nEquine Park\nNemo Farm Animal Hospital\nAmbulatory\nJanet L. Swanson Wildlife Hospital\nCornell Ruffian Equine Specialists\nServices & Specialties\nClinical Trials\nVeterinary Community\nCUHA rVet Connect Help\nCareers\nClinical Trials\nThank you for considering enrolling a pet in a clinical trial at Cornell. By participating, you are helping us to advance the health and well-being of animals and people.\nJoin our\nmailing list!\nSign up to be notified of new clinical trials.\nCornell Veterinary Clinical Trials\nCanine\nA New Drug for Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma in Dogs\nEffects of clonidine on stress for dogs at veterinary visits\nInvestigating the cause of blood clotting in dogs with IMHA\nRadiofrequency Therapy for Pain Management in Dogs\nSmart-Start Therapy for Canine B-Cell Lymphoma\nStudying Electrophysiology of the Sinus Node in Dogs who Need Pacemakers\nTraditional Versus Laparoscopic Castration in Dogs\nCanine, Equine\nStem Cell Therapy in Dogs and Horses\nStem Cell Therapy in Dogs and Horses\nFeline\nDietary Trial for Cats with Chronic Kidney Disease\nClinical Trials\nFrequently Asked Questions\nFaculty Resources\nVeterinarians\nGlossary of Terms\nClinical Trial Sponsors\nContact Us\nInterested in a specific clinical trial? Reach out to us.\nClinical trials are funded in part by the\nCornell Richard P. Riney Canine Health Center\nand the\nCornell Feline Health Center\n. Consider a gift to help more animals through clinical trials.\nDonate now\nContact Us\nFollow us on:\nResources\nWebmaster (support requests)\nWeb accessibility\nIT support requests\nIntranet\nCorporate and vendor policy\nGet Connected\nMedia\nUpcoming events\nContact us\nCareers\nCornell University ©2026\nPrivacy Policy\nEqual Education & Employment\nLand Acknowledgement",
